  "live_records": {
    "q-35500": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35500",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250470/assets/d1e5821252dd0634c6033a35247af033bcda8a96fa3733b65be52565a60ea3a6.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of $f(x).$ Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\,-2}f(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "As $x$ approaches $-2$ from the right, the function value $f(x)$ grows to infinity, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)=\\infty .\n$$\n\nHowever, as $x$ approaches $-2$ from the left, the function value $f(x)$ goes to $-\\infty $, and therefore\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -2}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
